{
  "summary": "Modernizes the OpenRC service scripts in contrib/init to match current OpenRC conventions and simplify configuration. It switches from /var/run to /run, relaxes the network dependency from 'need net' to 'use net', and replaces custom daemon options with standard OpenRC variables like command_user, SSD_NICELEVEL, and retry.",
  "problem": "The OpenRC init script in contrib/init uses outdated practices, redundant configuration variables, and a strict 'need net' dependency that forces bitcoind to restart whenever the host network service restarts.",
  "evidence": [
    "Originates from Gentoo bug report 987059 (https://bugs.gentoo.org/987059).",
    "OpenRC service script guide documentation cautions against 'need net' because it couples daemon lifetimes to network service restarts."
  ],
